      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.35,
      "end_seconds": 169.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.85,
      "end_seconds": 172.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Alright, and your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.91,
      "end_seconds": 177.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.61,
      "end_seconds": 181.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.88,
      "end_seconds": 188.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Yes, I had a mole taken off my arm, a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 203.19,
      "end_seconds": 212.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Blood pressure 128 over 70, heart rate 78. Temperature 37.0, oxygen saturation is 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.14,
      "end_seconds": 215.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.39,
      "end_seconds": 221.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.64,
      "end_seconds": 224.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.92,
      "end_seconds": 242.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "You are not pregnant by the urine test, the breasts express a little milk, and there is no visual field loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.28,
      "end_seconds": 247.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "all finished, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.28,
      "end_seconds": 270.77,
      "duration_seconds": 14.49,
      "text": "from what you've told me and what I found, I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at raised prolactin or a thyroid problem rather than stress or pituitary tumour"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.04,
      "end_seconds": 275.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.76,
      "end_seconds": 306.36,
      "duration_seconds": 29.6,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now raised prolactin or a thyroid problem rather than stress is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'll request an MRI of the pituitary, it'll help with possible prolactinoma. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'll request a prolactin and thyroid blood test, it'll help with galactorrhoea"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.99,
      "end_seconds": 308.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "right, understood"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 309.64,
      "end_seconds": 313.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "I've already done a pregnancy test, it's ready for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.72,
      "end_seconds": 336.03,
      "duration_seconds": 20.31,
      "text": "Thanks, that helps. Don't stress about stress as the cause, the tests will tell us. Let's get you seen by the endocrine clinic, I'll arrange the letter. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.8,
      "end_seconds": 339.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "That's fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.55,
      "end_seconds": 346.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "I'll want another look after the results. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.85,
      "end_seconds": 351.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
